              "elType": "widget",
              "widgetType": "text-editor",
              "settings": {
                "editor": "<p>Ramenhead is Cape Town's home of authentic Japanese ramen — a casual, walk-in ramen-ya in the heart of the city at Speaker's Corner, 37 Parliament Street. Every bowl begins with noodles made fresh in-house on the only Yamato noodle machine in Africa, paired with broths simmered for 48 hours until they carry real umami depth.</p><p>Behind the pass: Executive Chef Julia du Toit, with guidance from FYN Group's Peter Tempelhoff and Ashley Moss. The kitchen takes its cue from the ramen shops of Japan, building each bowl with authentic technique — and extending the same care to small plates, gyoza, and Japanese street food like okonomiyaki fries and chicken karaage. The bar pours sake from traditional masu cups, award-winning Japanese-inspired cocktails, and local and imported beers.</p><p>Open Tuesday through Saturday from 5 PM, with happy hour weekdays 5–7 PM (50% off all small plates and selected cocktails) and live music every Thursday. Walk-ins welcome; book a table via Dineplan. Outside seating available, weather dependent. No cash payments.</p>",
                "text_color": "#a6a39f",
                "align": "center",
                "typography_typography": "custom",
                "typography_font_family": "Poppins",
                "typography_font_size": {
